# T9AMAIL — TODO

## DO NOW — commit, then merge webproto into real app.py

**1. Commit current state first, before any further changes.**
Real `app.py` untouched (still the minimal `/`, `/test`, `/sendtest`
version), `webproto/` present with the proven nav+reply+send
prototype, this TODO.md included.

```
git add -A
git commit -m "Rollback point: webproto/ proven working (nav + real reply + real send), real app.py not yet merged"
git tag pre-webproto-merge
git push && git push --tags
```

The tag matters: repo history was already force-reset once before
(see handover v3) — a named tag makes "roll back to before the merge"
a one-command `git checkout pre-webproto-merge` rather than hunting
through `git log` for the right commit.

**2. Merge webproto/app.py's logic into the real app.py**, in place,
still binding port 80. As part of this same pass:
- Delete the stale `/sendtest` route (dead SMTP/msmtp code, superseded
  by Resend — see handover v3, "Sending mail" section).
- Delete `/test` (served its purpose proving the subprocess-from-Bottle
  pattern; no longer needed once real routes exist).
- Carry over: `/`, `/message`, `/view`, `/reply` (GET+POST), all real
  paths (headers.txt, MAILDIRS, send_json.sh subprocess call) already
  proven in webproto/app.py.

**3. Keep `webproto/` around for one more cycle** after the merge —
don't delete it in the same commit. It's the working reference/proof
of correctness if anything looks off in the merged version. Delete it
in a later, separate commit once the merged real app.py has been
confirmed solid (a few real days of use, or a specific test pass —
your call on the bar).

**4. Commit the merge separately**, clearly distinguished from the
rollback point commit above — e.g.
`git commit -m "Merge webproto nav/reply/send into real app.py, remove stale /test and /sendtest"`.

**5. Restart the real systemd service** (`t9amail-web.service`) once
the merge is deployed to the VPS via `git pull`, so it picks up the
new `app.py`.

